### BookVerse — manual API tests
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (or Thunder Client / Bruno).
### Click "Send Request" above each block. Cookies are stored & resent automatically.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = amr@example.com
@password = password123

### 1. Gateway health (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Signup (through the gateway) — sets sessionId + refreshToken cookies
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amr Nashaat",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Login — capture the access token for protected calls below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### grab the token out of the login response
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}

### 4. Example PROTECTED call (once the Book service exists)
###    The gateway verifies this token and injects x-user-* downstream.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. Refresh — uses the sessionId + refreshToken cookies automatically
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh

### 6. Logout — clears the session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### NEGATIVE TEST (run in a terminal, not here — auth-service isn't
### reachable from the host). Bypassing the gateway with no secret → 401:
###
###   docker compose exec -T gateway wget -S -O- --post-data='{}' \
###     --header='Content-Type: application/json' \
###     http://auth-service:3001/auth/login 2>&1 | head
